  "finding": "Every zero-S_ever persistence-off cell is a seed on which no world edge reaches the prediction floor of 5 inside a single cycle after the reset: 5 such cells, all with 0 admissible world edges and a maximum observed world-edge count of [3, 4]. The full observer/sleep path confirms it: all 5 zero cells serve 0 world edges. On the 7 non-zero cells the admissibility ceiling equals the observed S_ever exactly (T1/20612201 9=9; T1/20612202 3=3; T1/20612203 6=6; T1/20612206 5=5; T1b/20612209 1=1; T1b/20612211 3=3; T1b/20612213 3=3), and the two positive controls serve T1/20612201 9, T1b/20612211 3 world edges. The zero is a threshold consequence, not a failed measurement: the reset removes the cross-cycle counts that carry a world edge over the floor, and within-cycle repetition alone reaches 5 only on some seeds."
